arget\":{\"target_id\":\"sha256:a5c1daee7886f81d27b2b7718718fa7a3822b27a4bc1d057f99af01be7688a19\",\"display_path\":\"/Users/arndtgold/Documents/GitHub/ai-native-governance-delivery-framework\"},\"snapshot_id\":\"cc2701ee-83dc-438c-b194-ba91eac94520\",\"observed_as_of\":\"2026-10-18T09:48:53.852Z\",\"source_digest\":\"e97046a2611e51167ba1fbee88f910b522915d248d5de01c1201565ed91622a7\",\"state\":\"available\",\"code\":null,\"retryable\":false,\"data\":{\"context_id\":\"edac4ed5-d20a-43b2-b809-d7e861cf1aa1\",\"generation\":10,\"current\":true},\"authorizes\":false}}}}" sandboxId=source-66635fa41555d0fc sourceId=undefined
2026-10-18T09:49:07.783Z warning [mcp-app-sandbox] mcp_app_sandbox.console_message guestWebContentsId=7 initId=e747b727-0c04-470e-af03-1cbffe5ce709 level=warning lineNumber=105 message="AGDF_SDK_TRACE {\"trace_id\":\"283c44c1-6da7-4102-b6c7-a67fd1071980\",\"sequence\":30,\"observed_at\":\"2026-10-18T09:49:07.782Z\",\"direction\":\"out\",\"message\":{\"method\":\"ui/update-model-context\",\"params\":{\"structuredContent\":{\"schema_version\":\"1\",\"target\":{\"target_id\":\"sha256:a5c1daee7886f81d27b2b7718718fa7a3822b27a4bc1d057f99af01be7688a19\",\"display_path\":\"/Users/arndtgold/Documents/GitHub/ai-native-governance-delivery-framework\"},\"snapshot_id\":\"cc2701ee-83dc-438c-b194-ba91eac94520\",\"observed_as_of\":\"2026-10-18T09:48:53.852Z\",\"source_digest\":\"e97046a2611e51167ba1fbee88f910b522915d248d5de01c1201565ed91622a7\",\"run_id\":\"agdf-cockpit-plugin-integration-20261016-01\",\"revision_id\":\"945b1eb3-5b01-4189-960f-adda17e77851\",\"context_id\":\"edac4ed5-d20a-43b2-b809-d7e861cf1aa1\",\"generation\":10,\"prepared_at\":\"2026-10-18T09:49:07.533Z\",\"artefact\":{\"resource\":{\"resource_id\":\"7bf2fe6c-45a4-40a9-a3bc-463bd2b30b10\",\"run_id\":\"agdf-cockpit-plugin-integration-20261016-01\",\"type\":\"PRD\",\"path\":\".agdf/control/artefacts/agdf-cockpit-plugin-integration-20261016-01/PRD.md\",\"registered_reference\":\".agdf/control/artefacts/agdf-cockpit-plugin-integration-20261016-01/PRD.md\",\"status\":\"registered\"},\"format\":\"markdown\",\"content\":\"# PRD: Cockpit included in the AGDF plugin for Codex\\n\\nStatus: draft\\nGate: PRD\\nGate approval: open\\nBased on: approved UR\\nDate: 2026-10-16\\nOwner: Arndt Gold\\nTraceability contract: criteria-chain-v1\\n\\n## 1. Product Scope\\n\\nDeliver the existing Cockpit as part of the normal AGDF plugin installation in Codex. The user installs or updates AGDF and asks to open Cockpit for an established project; no separate Cockpit build, MCP registration or project configuration is required. The visible feature name is **Cockpit**, identified as part of AGDF where its host surface supports that identification. Technical tool/server identifiers remain an SD compatibility decision.\\n\\nInstallation and opening must distinguish supplied, enabled, connected and actually working states. A confirmed project is required for reading project data. Existing local users get a controlled transition, with verified replacement before retirement of a positively owned old connection. The product does not promise that host trust, permission or restart requirements disappear.\\n\\nFirst scope is Codex, including bounded local installation and fresh-host verification. Existing Claude work remains separate. Reuse the existing Cockpit content views and read/context semantics; no redesign is included.\\n\\n## 2. UX Intent And Success\\n\\n- ui_ux_impact: medium\\n- ux_intent_definition: UX_INTENT_DEFINITION.md; ready analytical input recorded by operation 5df7c8fb-4ef2-44a7-8fdd-3f14d1e62630\\n- primary_user_intent: Install AGDF once and open its Cockpit without setting up another server.\\n- success_signal: In a fresh Codex session, the installed plugin opens the Cockpit and displays canonical data for the intended project, with a verified single effective Cockpit path after legacy transition.\\n- primary_decision_or_action: Ask to open Cockpit; supply a project only when the conversation has not already established one unambiguously.\\n\\n## 3. Working Modes And Effective State\\n\\n| working_mode | effective_state | visible_state_types | effective_state_authority | primary_state_presentation_owner |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Clean install or update | Plugin supplies compatible Cockpit assets; discovery may require a fresh session | Installed, reconnect needed, available, preparation failed | Host installation/activation and existing AGDF runtime verification | Existing installer output and Codex plugin/MCP management |\\n| Open for confirmed project | A checked project binding and current source reads are established | Cockpit ready for named project, opening failed | Existing AGDF target and canonical read services | Cockpit tool result and existing view |\\n| Project unresolved or unavailable | No project data can be presented as a valid binding | Project needed, project unavailable, retry available | Existing AGDF target validation | Cockpit tool result; concise chat clarification on" sandboxId=source-66635fa41555d0fc sourceId=undefined
